SUMMARY
-------
Native SwiftUI parity of the web DevTools page — a thin tabbed shell:
PageContainer(title, subtitle) over a 5-tab TabNav (Fleet API · Telemetry ·
Infrastructure · Utilities · Reference), each tab hosting its section. Reproduced
1:1 with TSTabs + a TSRouteTransition keyed on the tab (web <FadeIn key={tab}>),
adaptive across macOS (regular) and iOS (compact/regular). Every section binds
through its own @Observable model (P1/S8), injected by DevToolsRouteRegistration.

Four of the five web devtools sections already have Apple parity components
(FleetApiSection, FleetTelemetryHealth, ClientUtilitiesSection,
ReferenceLinksSection — under apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views). The web devtools
"InfrastructureSection" (a grid of backend dev-tool cards) has NO dedicated Apple
component — the like-named feature-views component is the *system status* surface
(parity of features/system/components/status/InfrastructureSection.tsx). It is
therefore composed in-page (DevToolsInfrastructureSection) from the canonical
BackendTool parity component: db-stats, migration-status, an MQTT tool (BackendTool
+ topic/message inputs in its `extra` slot = web children), env-check, runtime-info
— in the exact web source order.

