NOTE ON PATHS / DESTINATION
---------------------------
- The generated prompt names apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/** as the output
  dir; the real project lays sibling admin pages under apps/apple/Sources/Features/
  Admin/** (see ApiPlaygroundPage, TeslaOrdersPage, …). Files were placed there so
  the XcodeGen app target (sources: Sources) compiles them. Verified present in the
  generated project + compiled (DevToolsPage.o, DevToolsInfrastructureSection.o,
  DevToolsRouteRegistration.o produced).
- The KMP Shared.xcframework was assembled via Gradle
  (:core:assembleSharedXCFramework, BUILD SUCCESSFUL) and staged to
  apps/apple/Frameworks. Its release slices are ios-arm64, ios-arm64-simulator,
  macos-arm64 — there is no x86_64 simulator slice. The build therefore targets the
  arm64 iOS Simulator (the native simulator arch on this Apple-silicon runner) via
  EXCLUDED_ARCHS=x86_64. A generic-destination build links arm64 cleanly and only
  the (unavailable) x86_64 slice fails to link — an arch-availability limit of the
  prebuilt vendor framework, not of this artifact's code.

